      "inferred_from": {
        "inference": "This sentence, which says how an ACDC is bound to its issuer's key state, has no keyword, and line 1673 adds that ACDCs \"are not directly signed by the Issuer\" but bound to the issuer's key state, which line 95 requires a validator to establish by KERI. A seal of the ACDC's most compact SAID on the trunk of that key state is therefore the only issuer commitment the normative text describes, but no keyword sentence obliges a validator to refuse an ACDC without one, so refusing it is inferred and graded SHOULD (generators/SPEC-ISSUES.md, A-G1). The keyworded line 1843 is not cited, because it sits in the IPEX section, which line 1797 declares non-normative.",
        "line": 1663,
        "quote": "To protect against later forgery in the event of a future compromise of the Issuer's signing keys, the Issuer must anchor an *issuance* proof digest seal to the ACDC in its KEL either directly or indirectly.",
        "section": "Binding to Key State at Time of ACDC State Change"
      },
      "level": "SHOULD",
      "note": "Decided at step 4 (no-commitment). Derivations: step 4 no-commitment: SHOULD, inferred, because line 95 makes the issuer's key state the KERI one, and lines 1663 and 1673 bind an ACDC to it only by a seal, which no keyword sentence obliges a validator to require (A-G1). Graded at the highest, over the derivations, of the level of each."
    }
